  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "Jeremy Corbell, a guest on podcast host Jesse Michels's show, says he has heard that many American journalists in the 1960s were secretly paid by the CIA, the US foreign intelligence agency. He ties this to Operation Mockingbird, the name given to that alleged arrangement, and says the journalists' names and what they were paid are now known. If true, it would mean the agency had a hand in what the public was told."
